<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Performance on Human-Verified Adversarial Attacks</h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluated our framework and all baselines against the majority-vote labels from our human study. The results across individual attack vectors are detailed in Table <a href="#A3.T12" title='Table 12 ‣ C.3 Performance on Human-Verified Adversarial Attacks ‣ Appendix C Human-Annotated "Gold Standard" Study ‣ CourtGuard: A Model-Agnostic Framework for Zero-Shot Policy Adaptation in LLM Safety' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T12" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A3.T12.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 12</span>: </span><span id="A3.T12.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Granular Attack Results (Acc/F1):<span id="A3.T12.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Performance across nine distinct adversarial attack methodologies.</span></span></figcaption>
